is K times R, the projection matrix and the point, can be simplified to just the calibration

46:30.900 --> 46:37.260
matrix times the camera already with our direction vector, so in the camera frame.

46:37.260 --> 46:42.900
So the mapping is basically the point in the camera frame times the calibration matrix

46:42.900 --> 46:46.180
gives me my image coordinate directly.

