53:37.360 --> 53:42.580
towards the first camera, I go along the unit vector and then how the second camera is rotated

53:42.580 --> 53:43.580
with respect to this.

53:43.580 --> 53:46.560
So there's also a way you can describe this.

53:46.560 --> 53:54.080
So the general parameterization uses a normalized direction vector b, so a vector b that has

53:54.080 --> 53:59.400
